502
00:32:29,416 --> 00:32:30,333
Like a threesome?

503
00:32:30,541 --> 00:32:32,208
No, idiot! Not a threesome!

504
00:32:32,375 --> 00:32:33,416
You're impossible!

505
00:32:33,958 --> 00:32:35,540
I just want to know

506
00:32:35,541 --> 00:32:39,250
whether he's in this relationship
because he genuinely wants to be.

507
00:32:39,958 --> 00:32:43,041
If you succeed, I'll get clarity.

508
00:32:44,083 --> 00:32:46,875
If you really want to test
whether he really loves you,

509
00:32:47,125 --> 00:32:49,790
wouldn't it be better
if you slept with someone

510
00:32:49,791 --> 00:32:51,249
and then see if he stays or not?

511
00:32:51,250 --> 00:32:53,000
But I love him.

512
00:32:53,500 --> 00:32:55,165
It's his feelings I'm unsure about.

513
00:32:55,166 --> 00:32:57,374
I want to give him the chance
to walk out of it,

514
00:32:57,375 --> 00:32:58,666
if that's what he wants.

515
00:32:59,708 --> 00:33:02,625
Is it his love you want to test
or his character?

516
00:33:03,583 --> 00:33:05,791
If he shows interest in me
on his own, I'll understand.

517
00:33:06,250 --> 00:33:10,415
But if I'm throwing myself at him
and he still doesn't respond,

518
00:33:10,416 --> 00:33:12,041
then either he's dead from the waist down

519
00:33:12,625 --> 00:33:15,375
or has superhuman self-control.

520
00:33:16,208 --> 00:33:18,166
Okay, let's say he doesn't respond.

521
00:33:19,291 --> 00:33:22,750
Who's to say he won't end up
falling for another girl someday?

522
00:33:24,000 --> 00:33:25,083
It doesn't work this way.

523
00:33:25,583 --> 00:33:28,207
Feelings don't stick forever.

524
00:33:28,208 --> 00:33:29,625
Nothing's permanent.

525
00:33:30,208 --> 00:33:31,416
They can always change.

526
00:33:33,791 --> 00:33:35,208
Why are you overthinking this?

527
00:33:36,791 --> 00:33:37,791
It's a fun challenge.

528
00:33:39,166 --> 00:33:40,375
What do you have to lose?

529
00:33:40,958 --> 00:33:42,000
Are you sure?

530
00:33:43,041 --> 00:33:44,665
Because this "fun challenge"

531
00:33:44,666 --> 00:33:46,957
could destroy your perfectly
good relationship.

532
00:33:46,958 --> 00:33:48,207
I must tell you that.

533
00:33:48,208 --> 00:33:49,083
I'm sure.

534
00:33:50,708 --> 00:33:52,458
This could complicate our friendship too.

535
00:33:55,041 --> 00:33:56,458
It's been ten years since we last met.

536
00:33:56,875 --> 00:33:58,374
We're not such good friends.

537
00:33:58,375 --> 00:33:59,375
Ouch!

538
00:34:01,833 --> 00:34:02,833
Okay!

539
00:34:06,875 --> 00:34:09,958
By the way, I don't handle rejection well.

540
00:34:11,250 --> 00:34:14,666
So, if he doesn't respond to my flirting,
which never happens, by the way,

541
00:34:15,791 --> 00:34:18,500
and my ego gets bruised,
don't blame me.

542
00:34:19,416 --> 00:34:20,333
I won't.

543
00:34:25,333 --> 00:34:29,750
Okay, how far does he need to slip
before you believe he doesn't love you?

544
00:34:30,250 --> 00:34:31,125
What do you mean?

545
00:34:31,541 --> 00:34:34,541
I mean… this far?

546
00:34:36,000 --> 00:34:37,000
This far?

547
00:34:38,041 --> 00:34:40,165
- Or all the way…
- Okay, okay, okay, enough!

548
00:34:40,166 --> 00:34:41,791
That's enough to give me clarity.

549
00:34:45,416 --> 00:34:46,333
Kunal!

550
00:34:47,000 --> 00:34:49,207
- Wine.
- Yeah, that's the right one.

551
00:34:49,208 --> 00:34:50,250
What are you two talking about?

552
00:34:50,708 --> 00:34:51,750
Negotiating your price.

553
00:34:52,708 --> 00:34:54,791
I said, now that we've found
a diamond, we might as well bid for it.

554
00:34:55,666 --> 00:34:56,916
We were fixing the price.

555
00:34:57,500 --> 00:34:59,291
I'm not a diamond. I'm Kohinoor.

556
00:35:00,083 --> 00:35:02,125
It's not that easy to own me.

557
00:35:03,875 --> 00:35:04,916
Good night, ladies.

558
00:35:06,625 --> 00:35:07,958
Sorry.
Good night.

559
00:35:08,250 --> 00:35:09,916
You are gonna have a really good night.

560
00:35:11,000 --> 00:35:12,124
Good night, baby.

561
00:35:12,125 --> 00:35:14,458
- Nice ass.
- Wait. Hold on a second.

562
00:35:27,500 --> 00:35:28,916
Ciao, my bellas!

563
00:35:30,541 --> 00:35:31,500
Hi.

564
00:35:32,375 --> 00:35:33,374
Slept well?

565
00:35:33,375 --> 00:35:36,083
- Yeah.
- I'm here to cuddle with my baby.

566
00:35:36,666 --> 00:35:39,749
I spent two years in the hostel,
waking up to her alarm in her arms.

567
00:35:39,750 --> 00:35:41,457
- I too want to cuddle with my baby.
- Oh my God!

568
00:35:41,458 --> 00:35:44,333
Guys, guys, time out! God!

569
00:35:46,666 --> 00:35:49,083
Baby… you're not ticklish?

570
00:35:49,625 --> 00:35:50,541
What?

571
00:35:54,000 --> 00:35:56,041
She's not, but I am.

572
00:36:01,875 --> 00:36:03,500
Don't worry, it's okay.

573
00:36:04,958 --> 00:36:06,916
What's the hurry, darling?

574
00:36:07,291 --> 00:36:08,750
She won't get jealous of me.

575
00:36:09,583 --> 00:36:11,582
- Right?
- I'll manage.

576
00:36:11,583 --> 00:36:12,707
She may not get jealous,

577
00:36:12,708 --> 00:36:15,375
but you can't handle all this hotness.

578
00:36:15,916 --> 00:36:16,833
Try me.

579
00:36:17,958 --> 00:36:18,875
Breakfast?

580
00:36:19,333 --> 00:36:20,999
Listen, I'll join you in some time.

581
00:36:21,000 --> 00:36:22,666
I have two emails to send before that.

582
00:36:22,875 --> 00:36:23,791
Okay.

583
00:36:24,041 --> 00:36:24,916
I'll join you.

584
00:36:26,041 --> 00:36:27,500
Okay. So…

585
00:36:30,833 --> 00:36:33,458
{\an8}DANCE CLASS
LEARN TO DANCE

586
00:36:35,666 --> 00:36:36,958
Okay, this will be fun.

587
00:36:58,375 --> 00:36:59,416
Breakfast!

588
00:37:02,250 --> 00:37:05,208
If you're vacationing with me,
you need to loosen up a lot, my friend.

589
00:37:05,875 --> 00:37:08,666
Two drinks in,
and I'm completely loosened up.

590
00:37:09,916 --> 00:37:10,916
Can't wait.

591
00:37:22,791 --> 00:37:25,166
I need a guy's perspective
on something.

592
00:37:25,625 --> 00:37:26,958
Ask away. I'm a guy.

593
00:37:27,833 --> 00:37:29,250
Unsolicited opinions are my thing.

594
00:37:30,875 --> 00:37:34,041
Is there such a thing as
too much passion?

595
00:37:39,791 --> 00:37:40,749
What?

596
00:37:40,750 --> 00:37:43,666
Well, my last relationship,
or whatever it was,

597
00:37:44,500 --> 00:37:47,208
ended because he thought
that's all I ever wanted.

598
00:37:49,958 --> 00:37:51,375
He should've been happy, right?

599
00:37:52,916 --> 00:37:53,875
What do you think?

600
00:37:56,000 --> 00:37:57,083
You're a <i>narbhakshi.</i>

601
00:37:57,625 --> 00:37:58,582
What's that?

602
00:37:58,583 --> 00:38:01,541
<i>"Nar"</i> means man. Me.

603
00:38:02,166 --> 00:38:06,249
<i>"Bhakshi"</i> means eater. That's you.

604
00:38:06,250 --> 00:38:08,375
No, no, I'm serious.
From a guy's perspective,

605
00:38:08,958 --> 00:38:11,332
is being passionate really a bad thing?

606
00:38:11,333 --> 00:38:13,916
And who passes on an opportunity

607
00:38:14,416 --> 00:38:17,041
to have a purely physical relationship?

608
00:38:20,833 --> 00:38:21,791
With me.

609
00:38:30,666 --> 00:38:31,583
Would you?

610
00:38:42,083 --> 00:38:43,083
- Boo!
- Oh!

611
00:38:43,625 --> 00:38:45,208
Baby! Where were you?

612
00:38:45,708 --> 00:38:46,791
I was waiting for you.

613
00:38:47,125 --> 00:38:49,707
- I was finalizing today's plan.
- Yeah?

614
00:38:49,708 --> 00:38:51,791
I've booked us a vineyard tour.

615
00:38:52,208 --> 00:38:54,500
I have no interest
in watching wine being made.

616
00:38:55,333 --> 00:38:57,625
I've planned an architecture tour.

617
00:39:00,541 --> 00:39:01,916
It's her holiday.
She gets to decide.

618
00:39:02,583 --> 00:39:04,416
No, baby, it's okay.

619
00:39:04,750 --> 00:39:06,250
I know you'll get bored.

620
00:39:07,625 --> 00:39:08,958
You go with her.

621
00:39:09,541 --> 00:39:12,000
I'll see you both at dinner.

622
00:39:13,333 --> 00:39:16,332
No, we're on this holiday together.
We'll do everything together.

623
00:39:16,333 --> 00:39:17,957
Don't be silly.
I'll come with you, baby.

624
00:39:17,958 --> 00:39:20,790
Baby, we can do things
separately for one day.

625
00:39:20,791 --> 00:39:22,083
What's the big deal?

626
00:39:22,333 --> 00:39:23,208
Really?

627
00:39:24,916 --> 00:39:26,125
- Yeah.
- Come here.

628
00:39:33,208 --> 00:39:34,208
Shall we?

629
00:39:41,166 --> 00:39:42,332
- Miss…
- How much?

630
00:39:42,333 --> 00:39:43,790
A coppola for your handsome boyfriend?

631
00:39:43,791 --> 00:39:44,832
- No, no, no.
- Yeah…

632
00:39:44,833 --> 00:39:46,833
- I'm… I'm not her…
- Yes.

633
00:39:48,333 --> 00:39:49,750
I'll take…

634
00:39:52,416 --> 00:39:53,415
I'll pay for it.

635
00:39:53,416 --> 00:39:54,875
- You'll give a discount?
- It's okay, it's okay.

636
00:39:55,833 --> 00:39:57,375
I've conned plenty of guys before.

637
00:39:58,166 --> 00:40:00,250
You can join that distinguished list too.

638
00:40:07,041 --> 00:40:09,708
You reacted to the idea
of being my boyfriend

639
00:40:10,625 --> 00:40:12,291
as if I'd insulted you.

640
00:40:14,250 --> 00:40:15,208
Am I really that bad?

641
00:40:16,250 --> 00:40:17,958
No! Not at all.

642
00:40:18,333 --> 00:40:21,500
I just didn't want you to feel awkward.

643
00:40:23,500 --> 00:40:25,166
Who knows if I'm even your type?

644
00:40:26,750 --> 00:40:27,833
You are.

645
00:40:38,000 --> 00:40:39,166
Isn't it crazy?

646
00:40:41,041 --> 00:40:43,916
If you crush these ordinary grapes
the right way…

647
00:40:44,708 --> 00:40:48,541
at the right temperature, under the right
conditions, in the right barrel,

648
00:40:49,541 --> 00:40:51,083
leave them alone long enough,

649
00:40:52,000 --> 00:40:53,166
and they become
something extraordinary.

650
00:40:54,416 --> 00:40:55,750
You know, it's not just grapes.

651
00:40:56,208 --> 00:40:59,916
Apples, pears, cherries…

652
00:41:02,458 --> 00:41:03,875
every fruit carries a little intoxication.

653
00:41:06,583 --> 00:41:08,250
So you are passionate about something.

654
00:41:10,208 --> 00:41:11,166
Of course.

655
00:41:11,625 --> 00:41:13,166
What made you think I'm not passionate?

656
00:41:16,375 --> 00:41:17,875
What else are you passionate about?

657
00:41:18,250 --> 00:41:19,291
Food!

658
00:41:20,166 --> 00:41:21,790
Eating it and cooking it.

659
00:41:21,791 --> 00:41:23,166
It's no different, really.

660
00:41:23,541 --> 00:41:26,290
The right ingredients, a little patience,
a little time.

661
00:41:26,291 --> 00:41:27,166
Magic.

662
00:41:29,583 --> 00:41:30,458
Come with me.

663
00:41:30,958 --> 00:41:32,000
So, what's next?

664
00:41:40,791 --> 00:41:41,915
- Cheers!
- Cheers!

665
00:41:41,916 --> 00:41:42,915
Hello.

666
00:41:42,916 --> 00:41:46,708
Starting off with a light-bodied red
for the lovely couple.

667
00:41:48,083 --> 00:41:49,791
Go ahead, say it.

668
00:41:50,166 --> 00:41:52,583
Tell him we're not a couple.
We're just friends.

669
00:41:53,083 --> 00:41:55,041
If Diya heard, she'd lose it.

670
00:41:55,375 --> 00:41:56,791
It's not like that.

671
00:41:57,875 --> 00:41:59,500
I didn't mean it like that
back then either.

672
00:41:59,875 --> 00:42:01,333
There you go with the decency.

673
00:42:01,791 --> 00:42:03,500
What's wrong with men these days?

674
00:42:08,375 --> 00:42:10,415
Earlier, if I went out for drinks
with a guy,

675
00:42:10,416 --> 00:42:13,915
the first thing on his mind was
getting me drunk

676
00:42:13,916 --> 00:42:15,250
and taking advantage of me.

677
00:42:17,000 --> 00:42:20,791
Little did they know, ten guys
like them would've gone down

678
00:42:21,000 --> 00:42:22,833
before I even got out of my seat.

679
00:42:24,291 --> 00:42:25,708
Let the others take advantage.

680
00:42:26,583 --> 00:42:28,457
I'm happy to bear your loss with you.

681
00:42:28,458 --> 00:42:31,500
Oh… I like this Kunal.

682
00:42:42,541 --> 00:42:45,791
<i>Even if you want to run away
You never find an escape route</i>

683
00:42:48,041 --> 00:42:51,833
<i>Anyone who embraces you
Even for a moment</i>

684
00:42:54,083 --> 00:42:57,791
<i>Lives an entire lifetime in that moment</i>

685
00:42:58,833 --> 00:43:02,041
<i>If something burns
The smoke always shows</i>

686
00:43:02,458 --> 00:43:06,165
<i>I'm so lost in you
I don't even know how anymore</i>

687
00:43:06,166 --> 00:43:07,083
Careful…

688
00:43:09,083 --> 00:43:10,833
or you'll fall in love with me.

689
00:43:15,458 --> 00:43:17,208
It was a joke, man!

690
00:43:18,708 --> 00:43:20,291
There goes my fantasy!

691
00:43:20,708 --> 00:43:22,625
Car breaks down on a highway.

692
00:43:22,916 --> 00:43:24,333
I'm stranded.

693
00:43:24,958 --> 00:43:28,625
And a dreamy man plays the guitar
to entertain me.

694
00:43:30,291 --> 00:43:35,125
Oh, I forgot to ask Diya
where we're meeting for dinner.

695
00:43:35,375 --> 00:43:36,541
- One second.
- What's the hurry?

696
00:43:39,958 --> 00:43:41,625
Live in the moment, my friend.

697
00:43:44,916 --> 00:43:46,666
Come here. Sit.
Sit down.

698
00:43:47,625 --> 00:43:51,541
I don't know about those ten guys
you've been with before…

699
00:43:52,541 --> 00:43:54,416
but you've definitely folded.

700
00:43:54,958 --> 00:43:55,957
No.

701
00:43:55,958 --> 00:43:57,083
Here, drink this water.

702
00:43:58,541 --> 00:44:02,541
My legs aren't strong enough
to carry you back.

703
00:44:03,375 --> 00:44:04,916
- At least try.
- Go on, drink it.

704
00:44:11,000 --> 00:44:11,958
Thank you.

705
00:44:26,291 --> 00:44:27,208
Anshul!

706
00:44:27,791 --> 00:44:28,791
Goosebumps.

707
00:44:30,541 --> 00:44:32,040
Don't make any plans tomorrow.

708
00:44:32,041 --> 00:44:33,666
- We're going on a road trip.
- Okay.

709
00:44:35,166 --> 00:44:36,375
I'll just freshen up and come.

710
00:44:37,458 --> 00:44:38,875
Wait. I'll come too.

711
00:44:39,458 --> 00:44:40,416
One second.

712
00:44:42,125 --> 00:44:43,041
Nothing!

713
00:44:43,250 --> 00:44:45,665
I went at him like a sizzling hot dish,

714
00:44:45,666 --> 00:44:48,833
and he kept rejecting me like
yesterday's stale leftovers.

715
00:44:50,000 --> 00:44:51,166
What's wrong with him?

716
00:44:51,333 --> 00:44:53,165
Seriously, what is wrong with him?

717
00:44:53,166 --> 00:44:54,624
Give it time.

718
00:44:54,625 --> 00:44:55,875
Maybe try harder.

719
00:44:56,541 --> 00:44:58,290
You know, I think he's not responding

720
00:44:58,291 --> 00:45:01,166
because he doesn't want
to seem like a player or a cheater.

721
00:45:03,041 --> 00:45:04,874
You'll have to nudge a little too.

722
00:45:04,875 --> 00:45:06,208
But what do I do?

723
00:45:06,750 --> 00:45:08,707
Maybe just try and push him away.

724
00:45:08,708 --> 00:45:11,790
Get him out of this
lovey-dovey holiday zone.

725
00:45:11,791 --> 00:45:12,874
- Do something!
- Okay, okay!

726
00:45:12,875 --> 00:45:13,791
Come on, Diya!

727
00:45:15,666 --> 00:45:17,957
Why do girls always go
to the bathroom together?

728
00:45:17,958 --> 00:45:20,583
Do your pee cycles sync too?

729
00:45:22,875 --> 00:45:24,833
Could you think before you speak for once?

730
00:45:28,666 --> 00:45:32,082
Baby, I just said pee cycle--

731
00:45:32,083 --> 00:45:33,458
Everything's a joke to you!

732
00:45:33,875 --> 00:45:36,750
At least look around
before blurting things out!

733
00:45:37,166 --> 00:45:38,625
It's okay, relax.

734
00:45:38,875 --> 00:45:40,041
It's just me.

735
00:45:40,708 --> 00:45:42,041
What's the big deal?

736
00:45:44,041 --> 00:45:46,250
Should we order?
I'm so hungry.

737
00:45:46,666 --> 00:45:47,875
Baby, you order.

738
00:45:48,583 --> 00:45:49,666
You know this stuff better.

739
00:45:51,958 --> 00:45:52,958
Pass me the menu.

740
00:45:53,666 --> 00:45:55,083
You handle his order. I'll handle mine.

741
00:45:57,500 --> 00:45:58,416
Please.

742
00:45:59,708 --> 00:46:00,625
Sure.

743
00:46:04,000 --> 00:46:05,875
You know what I would
love to have right now?

744
00:46:06,375 --> 00:46:07,333
<i>Kadhi chawal.</i>

745
00:46:09,750 --> 00:46:11,999
That's the only thing I miss from India.

746
00:46:12,000 --> 00:46:13,750
You should've told me!

747
00:46:14,583 --> 00:46:16,166
I would've made <i>kadhi chawal</i> for her.

748
00:46:17,166 --> 00:46:18,750
When was the last time you cooked?

749
00:46:21,125 --> 00:46:22,750
"I would've made it," he says!

750
00:46:32,875 --> 00:46:34,291
Sorry, guys. Sorry.

751
00:46:49,750 --> 00:46:51,583
Kunal, shut the window!

752
00:46:53,541 --> 00:46:54,875
Baby, why are you sleeping here?

753
00:46:55,291 --> 00:46:57,125
- I'm really sorry about last night--
- Shut up!

754
00:46:57,250 --> 00:46:58,666
My head is exploding.

755
00:46:59,541 --> 00:47:01,000
Ciao, my bellas!

756
00:47:03,041 --> 00:47:04,833
Ready for the trip of your lives, guys?

757
00:47:06,958 --> 00:47:08,165
What?

758
00:47:08,166 --> 00:47:09,665
Her head's exploding.

759
00:47:09,666 --> 00:47:11,166
She gets bad migraines.

760
00:47:12,541 --> 00:47:15,040
I think we might have to cancel the trip.

761
00:47:15,041 --> 00:47:16,624
- No!
- Yeah!

762
00:47:16,625 --> 00:47:19,041
- Kunal!
- Sorry. Sorry, baby.

763
00:47:21,125 --> 00:47:23,000
I booked such a sexy villa.

764
00:47:23,583 --> 00:47:25,708
And it's all non-refundable, you know?

765
00:47:26,833 --> 00:47:28,249
But it's okay.

766
00:47:28,250 --> 00:47:29,500
It's just money. It's fine.

767
00:47:30,625 --> 00:47:32,375
No, no, it's not okay.

768
00:47:32,500 --> 00:47:35,083
