01:38:16,708 --> 01:38:19,790
We're thinking that we'll do
a combined party.

1513
01:38:19,791 --> 01:38:23,332
Nice, chill scenes where
everyone enjoys themselves.

1514
01:38:23,333 --> 01:38:25,416
- What…
- Whose stupid idea is this?

1515
01:38:28,083 --> 01:38:28,958
Seriously?

1516
01:38:29,208 --> 01:38:31,083
No, but it's nice, right?

1517
01:38:31,583 --> 01:38:33,041
What's a "youngsters' party"?

1518
01:38:43,416 --> 01:38:45,083
Hello, everybody!

1519
01:38:46,708 --> 01:38:48,875
Bachelor party for what?
What's the big deal?

1520
01:38:49,208 --> 01:38:51,000
We've known each other forever.

1521
01:38:52,250 --> 01:38:53,374
Yeah.

1522
01:38:53,375 --> 01:38:54,791
Come on, guys.
It was my idea.

1523
01:38:55,958 --> 01:38:56,916
Want something to drink?

1524
01:38:58,041 --> 01:38:58,999
Anybody else?

1525
01:38:59,000 --> 01:38:59,957
- Me.
- I'm good.

1526
01:38:59,958 --> 01:39:01,458
Smile, guys! Come on!

1527
01:39:01,750 --> 01:39:03,040
Yay, bachelor party!

1528
01:39:03,041 --> 01:39:04,458
Let's have a devotional gathering, guys!

1529
01:39:05,041 --> 01:39:07,582
Look, you'll have to respect
the traditions.

1530
01:39:07,583 --> 01:39:08,874
And all of them.
Right, guys?

1531
01:39:08,875 --> 01:39:09,832
- Right.
- Correct.

1532
01:39:09,833 --> 01:39:10,874
And as your bridesmaid,

1533
01:39:10,875 --> 01:39:13,374
it's my duty to throw you a bachelorette.

1534
01:39:13,375 --> 01:39:16,499
- So plan the youngsters' party.
- What even is a youngsters' party?

1535
01:39:16,500 --> 01:39:18,124
- Who does that? Come on, guys!
- Baby.

1536
01:39:18,125 --> 01:39:19,416
- Youngsters…
- Yeah!

1537
01:39:20,500 --> 01:39:23,375
Here's what I think.
If we're doing all the rituals anyway,

1538
01:39:23,500 --> 01:39:25,375
might as well do this one too.

1539
01:39:26,375 --> 01:39:28,458
- What do you think?
- No, I…

1540
01:39:28,916 --> 01:39:31,040
- Please, Diya…
- Come on, Diya!

1541
01:39:31,041 --> 01:39:33,165
- Come on!
- Please!

1542
01:39:33,166 --> 01:39:34,415
- Come on!
- Please.

1543
01:39:34,416 --> 01:39:36,207
- Come on!
- Come on!

1544
01:39:36,208 --> 01:39:37,374
- Please…
- Fine!

1545
01:39:37,375 --> 01:39:39,332
- Fine! Fine!
- Okay!

1546
01:39:39,333 --> 01:39:40,500
I love you!

1547
01:39:44,125 --> 01:39:46,375
For letting me throw
the best party for her!

1548
01:39:48,375 --> 01:39:49,750
- Wow!
- Yeah!

1549
01:39:49,916 --> 01:39:50,833
You're welcome.

1550
01:39:51,416 --> 01:39:52,666
I didn't say "thank you," idiot.

1551
01:39:53,333 --> 01:39:54,208
I said, "Love you."

1552
01:39:56,125 --> 01:39:58,000
It won't kill you to say, "Love you too."

1553
01:40:02,041 --> 01:40:03,000
Okay. I love you too.

1554
01:40:03,625 --> 01:40:04,541
Happy?

1555
01:40:10,041 --> 01:40:12,124
Should we plan this, guys? Yeah?

1556
01:40:12,125 --> 01:40:13,540
This is a great idea. I love it.

1557
01:40:13,541 --> 01:40:15,208
- Thank you for the farmhouse, but…
- But, but…

1558
01:40:19,208 --> 01:40:21,082
Let's go, boys. Let's go.

1559
01:40:21,083 --> 01:40:22,166
Time to party!

1560
01:40:29,291 --> 01:40:30,208
What are you doing here?

1561
01:40:38,708 --> 01:40:39,791
Remember the vineyard?

1562
01:40:40,875 --> 01:40:41,750
Yeah.

1563
01:40:44,250 --> 01:40:45,208
Have fun.

1564
01:40:47,583 --> 01:40:48,541
Where are you going?

1565
01:40:50,791 --> 01:40:52,000
I just came to give you this.

1566
01:40:54,416 --> 01:40:56,583
I have another party to set up.

1567
01:40:57,041 --> 01:40:58,250
Won't you stay for a drink?

1568
01:41:00,208 --> 01:41:01,208
I'll stay…

1569
01:41:02,625 --> 01:41:03,750
but what will you tell Diya?

1570
01:41:04,208 --> 01:41:05,166
One drink.

1571
01:41:08,458 --> 01:41:09,375
Okay.

1572
01:41:14,875 --> 01:41:17,000
I've never seen you this quiet.

1573
01:41:22,208 --> 01:41:23,125
What's wrong?

1574
01:41:28,166 --> 01:41:29,041
Nothing.

1575
01:41:31,708 --> 01:41:32,583
It's nice.

1576
01:41:38,000 --> 01:41:41,500
Never thought my love could
stress someone out like this.

1577
01:41:43,208 --> 01:41:50,208
I always thought the man I loved would
be thrilled to know I loved him.

1578
01:41:54,583 --> 01:41:58,166
If it's bothering you so much,
just forget I said anything.

1579
01:41:59,833 --> 01:42:00,875
How can I forget?

1580
01:42:04,291 --> 01:42:06,291
These aren't things you forget, Ally.

1581
01:42:10,500 --> 01:42:14,040
You've said "I love you,"

1582
01:42:14,041 --> 01:42:17,125
but I don't think you even know
what love really is.

1583
01:42:20,250 --> 01:42:21,166
Okay.

1584
01:42:21,791 --> 01:42:24,916
Maybe I'm not familiar with
all this "textbook wisdom."

1585
01:42:28,500 --> 01:42:32,833
But I know what I feel for you…

1586
01:42:35,333 --> 01:42:36,291
is love.

1587
01:42:37,875 --> 01:42:39,333
You love me,

1588
01:42:41,291 --> 01:42:43,666
but it doesn't bother you that…

1589
01:42:45,625 --> 01:42:46,666
we're not together?

1590
01:42:47,583 --> 01:42:48,541
Of course it bothers me.

1591
01:42:50,041 --> 01:42:51,166
But what can I do?

1592
01:42:53,875 --> 01:42:56,750
And I love you…

1593
01:42:59,500 --> 01:43:02,666
but you never said you feel the same.

1594
01:43:14,333 --> 01:43:17,499
<i>Hear my prayers, before you I bow alone</i>

1595
01:43:17,500 --> 01:43:20,415
Okay then… I guess that's my cue.

1596
01:43:20,416 --> 01:43:23,457
<i>Bulleya, I've forgotten the way back home</i>

1597
01:43:23,458 --> 01:43:26,916
Ally, Ally, Ally!
Where are you going?

1598
01:43:27,958 --> 01:43:30,833
Stay with us.
We'll have the night of a lifetime.

1599
01:43:31,625 --> 01:43:32,957
Thanks for the offer, man,

1600
01:43:32,958 --> 01:43:35,250
but I've got bridesmaid duty.
Sorry.

1601
01:43:35,791 --> 01:43:37,499
Ally, you sure I can't convince you?

1602
01:43:37,500 --> 01:43:39,083
- Diya's gonna kill me, bro.
- Hey!

1603
01:43:40,250 --> 01:43:41,708
Think before you speak.

1604
01:43:43,375 --> 01:43:45,583
You're not a kid.
Is that any way to talk to a girl?

1605
01:43:45,958 --> 01:43:47,332
"Night of a lifetime!"

1606
01:43:47,333 --> 01:43:49,415
I meant at the party.

1607
01:43:49,416 --> 01:43:52,040
Then rehearse it in your head
before you say it!

1608
01:43:52,041 --> 01:43:53,665
Kunal… it's okay.

1609
01:43:53,666 --> 01:43:55,499
I'm sure he didn't mean that.

1610
01:43:55,500 --> 01:43:56,750
- Idiot!
- It's fine.

1611
01:43:57,083 --> 01:43:58,625
We're good, okay?

1612
01:43:59,875 --> 01:44:01,249
- Bye.
- Bye.

1613
01:44:01,250 --> 01:44:06,125
<i>Bulleya, I've forgotten the way back home</i>

1614
01:44:06,250 --> 01:44:11,624
<i>Hear my prayers, before you I bow alone</i>

1615
01:44:11,625 --> 01:44:12,625
<i>Bulleya…</i>

1616
01:44:14,000 --> 01:44:15,832
- Guys!
- There's a lot!

1617
01:44:15,833 --> 01:44:16,958
That's it?

1618
01:44:18,541 --> 01:44:19,958
Come on, guys, get up!

1619
01:44:20,083 --> 01:44:21,458
Give me, give me, give me.

1620
01:44:27,208 --> 01:44:28,749
- Oh God…
- What are you doing?

1621
01:44:28,750 --> 01:44:29,707
Give me my phone.

1622
01:44:29,708 --> 01:44:31,290
- Absolutely not.
- Ally…

1623
01:44:31,291 --> 01:44:33,791
You can talk to Kunal
for the rest of your life.

1624
01:44:34,333 --> 01:44:37,082
Tonight, you're single.

1625
01:44:37,083 --> 01:44:38,500
And you're with me.

1626
01:44:38,916 --> 01:44:39,958
Ally…

1627
01:44:40,291 --> 01:44:42,958
Smile, my love.
We're not mourning.

1628
01:44:43,791 --> 01:44:45,750
We're kicking off
your wedding celebrations.

1629
01:44:46,291 --> 01:44:47,166
See?

1630
01:44:55,750 --> 01:44:58,000
<i>The number you are calling
is not answering.</i>

1631
01:45:12,375 --> 01:45:17,875
<i>Bulleya, I've forgotten the way back home</i>

1632
01:45:18,000 --> 01:45:23,790
<i>Hear my prayers, before you I bow alone</i>

1633
01:45:23,791 --> 01:45:29,290
<i>Bulleya, I've forgotten the way back home</i>

1634
01:45:29,291 --> 01:45:32,374
<i>Hear my prayers</i>

1635
01:45:32,375 --> 01:45:34,957
- Nice.
<i>- Before you I bow alone</i>

1636
01:45:34,958 --> 01:45:40,665
<i>It kept wandering, this lost drifter</i>

1637
01:45:40,666 --> 01:45:43,124
- Lift.
<i>- My poor heart is</i>

1638
01:45:43,125 --> 01:45:46,165
- Careful!
<i>- Caught on you forever.</i>

1639
01:45:46,166 --> 01:45:51,916
<i>Lift this veil of silence at last</i>

1640
01:45:52,041 --> 01:45:57,540
<i>Such a moment may never come back</i>

1641
01:45:57,541 --> 01:46:01,749
<i>Fulfill the longing of my heart</i>

1642
01:46:01,750 --> 01:46:02,666
Stop the car.

1643
01:46:04,666 --> 01:46:05,541
Stop the car.

1644
01:46:06,083 --> 01:46:08,999
- What happened?
<i>- Before I fall apart…</i>

1645
01:46:09,000 --> 01:46:12,125
<i>Bulleya, I've forgotten the way…</i>

1646
01:46:23,583 --> 01:46:24,625
What did you think?

1647
01:46:28,250 --> 01:46:29,458
You'd say "I love you…"

1648
01:46:31,416 --> 01:46:32,791
and I'd leave Diya?

1649
01:46:36,375 --> 01:46:37,500
Leave a girl…

1650
01:46:38,833 --> 01:46:42,541
four days before her wedding?

1651
01:46:44,916 --> 01:46:46,583
Embarrass her in front of everyone?

1652
01:46:50,833 --> 01:46:52,583
Just because you think…

1653
01:46:55,041 --> 01:46:57,125
you and I are better together?

1654
01:47:01,916 --> 01:47:03,000
You don't think so?

1655
01:47:11,708 --> 01:47:12,583
No, I don't.

1656
01:47:19,375 --> 01:47:20,250
You sure?

1657
01:47:21,583 --> 01:47:22,500
I'm sure.

1658
01:47:31,875 --> 01:47:35,875
You can't leave Diya,
but you can at least be honest.

1659
01:47:51,875 --> 01:47:54,708
- I'll open it, Kunal, just…
- No, I'm good…

1660
01:47:58,416 --> 01:47:59,708
What are you two doing together?

1661
01:48:00,458 --> 01:48:01,833
I called you, baby.

1662
01:48:03,375 --> 01:48:05,500
You didn't answer,
so she came to get me.

1663
01:48:05,916 --> 01:48:06,916
Where's my phone?

1664
01:48:07,625 --> 01:48:09,624
Oh, shit! I'm so sorry.

1665
01:48:09,625 --> 01:48:11,499
I took it from you
and dropped it in my bag.

1666
01:48:11,500 --> 01:48:13,165
- I didn't realize.
- Yeah, right.

1667
01:48:13,166 --> 01:48:15,583
- Yeah, right.
- I saw your missed call.

1668
01:48:17,250 --> 01:48:19,250
I called you so many times,
but you never answered.

1669
01:48:20,375 --> 01:48:22,416
So, I asked her to come pick me up.

1670
01:48:22,541 --> 01:48:23,666
Why didn't you tell me?

1671
01:48:24,583 --> 01:48:26,666
You were asleep.
I didn't want to bother you.

1672
01:48:27,083 --> 01:48:28,749
He just needed a ride, so I picked him up.

1673
01:48:28,750 --> 01:48:29,999
You should've told me!

1674
01:48:30,000 --> 01:48:31,541
She just told you, didn't she?

1675
01:48:34,625 --> 01:48:36,166
She didn't want to bother you.

1676
01:48:37,416 --> 01:48:38,291
What is wrong with you?

1677
01:49:22,791 --> 01:49:23,666
Hey!

1678
01:49:23,833 --> 01:49:24,874
Hey!

1679
01:49:24,875 --> 01:49:25,833
Can you…

1680
01:49:27,625 --> 01:49:28,582
Sorry.

1681
01:49:28,583 --> 01:49:31,250
Could you move into a hotel for tonight?

1682
01:49:32,083 --> 01:49:33,000
Why?

1683
01:49:33,666 --> 01:49:35,833
It's our last night in this house
before the wedding.

1684
01:49:35,958 --> 01:49:38,000
We'll no longer be
boyfriend and girlfriend.

1685
01:49:38,166 --> 01:49:39,208
We'll be husband and wife.

1686
01:49:39,833 --> 01:49:43,500
I just want to spend this last day…

1687
01:49:46,583 --> 01:49:47,875
alone with him.

1688
01:49:52,458 --> 01:49:54,750
If you're insecure, just say it.

1689
01:49:55,833 --> 01:49:58,541
Why? Is there something
to be insecure about?

1690
01:49:59,458 --> 01:50:00,416
Maybe.

1691
01:50:03,333 --> 01:50:04,375
You were right.

1692
01:50:05,083 --> 01:50:07,666
You don't handle rejection gracefully.

1693
01:50:08,750 --> 01:50:12,791
But I didn't think you'd stoop this low.

1694
01:50:14,958 --> 01:50:16,416
What are you trying to prove?

1695
01:50:16,916 --> 01:50:18,875
I don't need to prove anything to anyone.

1696
01:50:21,750 --> 01:50:23,250
I just love Kunal.

1697
01:50:24,875 --> 01:50:25,916
I love him.

1698
01:50:26,500 --> 01:50:27,833
What? No…

1699
01:50:28,833 --> 01:50:31,125
And I've already told him how I feel.

1700
01:50:32,958 --> 01:50:34,083
He didn't tell you?

1701
01:50:37,500 --> 01:50:38,500
Oops.

1702
01:50:43,041 --> 01:50:44,083
What did he say?

1703
01:50:47,708 --> 01:50:49,583
Isn't it sad that you have to ask me?

1704
01:50:51,625 --> 01:50:52,916
But actually that's the point.

1705
01:50:53,458 --> 01:50:55,750
First love isn't always true love, Diya.

1706
01:50:57,500 --> 01:50:59,375
You met him first. That's your luck.

1707
01:51:00,083 --> 01:51:02,208
Doesn't mean you're right for him.

1708
01:51:02,958 --> 01:51:06,000
Maybe I found him too late,
but I love him.

1709
01:51:07,000 --> 01:51:09,791
So I'm supposed to sacrifice my love
just because you met him first?

1710
01:51:10,458 --> 01:51:11,666
How does that make sense?

1711
01:51:12,208 --> 01:51:13,416
Especially when he…

1712
01:51:23,333 --> 01:51:24,208
Don't worry.

1713
01:51:25,375 --> 01:51:26,416
I'm not a home-wrecker.

1714
01:51:27,625 --> 01:51:30,000
But I still have the right
to stop this wedding.

1715
01:51:32,208 --> 01:51:33,958
And till the vows are taken,
I'm not giving up.

1716
01:51:37,125 --> 01:51:38,291
If he takes them with you, he's yours.

1717
01:51:39,875 --> 01:51:41,041
If I can stop them, he's mine.

1718
01:51:43,666 --> 01:51:45,375
I've known Kunal since we were kids.

1719
01:51:47,083 --> 01:51:49,333
For as long as I can remember,
we've been together.

1720
01:51:50,875 --> 01:51:53,165
You've known him for a month.

1721
01:51:53,166 --> 01:51:54,958
That's not love.

1722
01:51:55,916 --> 01:51:57,125
That's confusion.

1723
01:51:59,500 --> 01:52:02,583
Fine, so you told Kunal you love him.

1724
01:52:03,125 --> 01:52:04,875
But did you also tell him

1725
01:52:05,208 --> 01:52:07,249
you've been trying to stop this wedding?

1726
01:52:07,250 --> 01:52:08,208
Oh, wait!

1727
01:52:08,875 --> 01:52:10,958
You wouldn't risk looking so bad

1728
01:52:11,791 --> 01:52:14,291
before the man you love.

1729
01:52:15,875 --> 01:52:17,207
You're right.

1730
01:52:17,208 --> 01:52:20,500
Can't look so bad
in the eyes of the guy

1731
01:52:20,833 --> 01:52:22,208
you are about to marry.

1732
01:52:23,541 --> 01:52:26,000
Does Kunal know you asked me
to seduce him?

1733
01:52:32,416 --> 01:52:33,416
No?

1734
01:52:34,625 --> 01:52:36,583
Our friendship has no value for you.

1735
01:52:38,583 --> 01:52:39,791
We're not such good friends.

1736
01:52:44,041 --> 01:52:46,291
You're up already?
How are you feeling?

1737
01:52:47,083 --> 01:52:48,458
A bad one, baby.

1738
01:52:49,041 --> 01:52:50,041
I need my…

1739
01:52:50,333 --> 01:52:52,791
Sit back.
I'll make your hangover cure.

1740
01:52:53,416 --> 01:52:54,625
Already made one.

1741
01:52:55,125 --> 01:52:56,125
My special recipe.

1742
01:52:56,875 --> 01:52:59,041
Mine's worked on him for years.

1743
01:52:59,458 --> 01:53:01,790
If he tries mine,
he'll ask for it for years.

1744
01:53:01,791 --> 01:53:02,666
Come, have it.

1745
01:53:03,708 --> 01:53:05,750
Have it.

1746
01:53:06,125 --> 01:53:07,041
Like it?

1747
01:53:07,708 --> 01:53:09,415
- Better than the usual one, right?
- Water…

1748
01:53:09,416 --> 01:53:10,958
Oh, my poor baby!

1749
01:53:12,125 --> 01:53:15,000
Just lie down for ten minutes.
You'll be fine.

1750
01:53:16,416 --> 01:53:18,915
So, this time the booze was dodgy,
or it just didn't hit?

1751
01:53:18,916 --> 01:53:21,415
No chance of the booze being dodgy.

1752
01:53:21,416 --> 01:53:24,125
I specially got him
his favorite wine from Sicily.

1753
01:53:26,583 --> 01:53:31,208
Remember when you ditched us
and we went on our vineyard "date"?

1754
01:53:32,125 --> 01:53:33,250
We just fell in love…

1755
01:53:34,666 --> 01:53:35,750
with the wine.

1756
01:53:35,958 --> 01:53:36,833
Too good, right?

1757
01:53:37,916 --> 01:53:40,375
No matter how good
or special the booze is,

1758
01:53:40,583 --> 01:53:41,833
or where it's from,

1759
01:53:41,958 --> 01:53:44,250
the high wears off by morning.

1760
01:53:44,416 --> 01:53:45,583
After that,

1761
01:53:45,833 --> 01:53:48,249
only my hangover cure works.
Have it.

1762
01:53:48,250 --> 01:53:49,999
- Don't be jealous, baby.
- It's okay.

1763
01:53:50,000 --> 01:53:51,791
Being your bridesmaid was your gift.

1764
01:53:52,208 --> 01:53:53,541
But I had to give him something too.

1765
01:53:53,833 --> 01:53:56,041
Someone has to attend
to this poor child.

1766
01:53:56,416 --> 01:53:58,458
He gets plenty of attention.

1767
01:53:59,000 --> 01:54:00,166
And I'm not jealous.

1768
01:54:00,583 --> 01:54:02,416
Oh, right! I forgot.

1769
01:54:02,833 --> 01:54:04,166
This "diya" has no flame.

1770
01:54:04,958 --> 01:54:08,125
No light. No warmth.

1771
01:54:08,916 --> 01:54:09,916
It's just there.

1772
01:54:10,750 --> 01:54:12,375
- No baby. It's okay.
- Come on, get ready quickly.

1773
01:54:12,583 --> 01:54:13,874
We need to go shopping.

1774
01:54:13,875 --> 01:54:14,791
Shopping for what?

1775
01:54:16,750 --> 01:54:17,833
For your gift.

1776
01:54:18,208 --> 01:54:19,083
It's a surprise.

1777
01:54:20,958 --> 01:54:22,957
It's a surprise.
Come, come.

1778
01:54:22,958 --> 01:54:24,957
- I don't need any surprises! Kunal!
- What would you do without me?

1779
01:54:24,958 --> 01:54:25,915
Come.

1780
01:54:25,916 --> 01:54:26,791
Go get ready.

1781
01:54:31,666 --> 01:54:33,416
You think only you can surprise people?

1782
01:54:34,291 --> 01:54:35,416
Like the engagement ring?

1783
01:54:37,000 --> 01:54:39,125
You should've seen his face.

1784
01:54:39,916 --> 01:54:41,333
He was so not ready for it.

1785
01:54:44,125 --> 01:54:45,625
I'll go get ready, okay?

1786
01:55:13,916 --> 01:55:15,625
How will you know just by holding it up?

1787
01:55:16,291 --> 01:55:17,166
Come.

1788
01:55:19,833 --> 01:55:20,833
Help me out.

1789
01:55:45,541 --> 01:55:46,583
You okay?

1790
01:56:01,041 --> 01:56:02,583
That's my boy.

1791
01:56:07,583 --> 01:56:08,458
Cheers.

1792
01:56:14,333 --> 01:56:15,208
Papa…

1793
01:56:17,208 --> 01:56:19,958
How long have you and Mom been together?

1794
01:56:22,500 --> 01:56:23,750
Around 34 or 35 years.

1795
01:56:29,750 --> 01:56:32,750
In all these years,
did you ever feel someone else

1796
01:56:35,250 --> 01:56:37,916
might've been better for either of you?

1797
01:56:40,125 --> 01:56:42,666
It was a perfect match!

1798
01:56:45,250 --> 01:56:49,416
In fact, your mother should thank God.

1799
01:56:49,875 --> 01:56:52,166
Where'd she find a better man than me?

1800
01:56:52,291 --> 01:56:53,916
Someone who's still putting up with her?!

1801
01:57:07,625 --> 01:57:11,374
Son, pre-wedding jitters, getting nervous,
and having doubts

1802
01:57:11,375 --> 01:57:12,875
are completely normal.

1803
01:57:14,041 --> 01:57:15,958
Have a couple of drinks and sleep it off.

1804
01:57:17,041 --> 01:57:18,540
Tomorrow morning,
we set off for Chandigarh,

1805
01:57:18,541 --> 01:57:20,500
and we'll play <i>antakshari</i> all the way
till we reach.

1806
01:57:21,416 --> 01:57:26,000
And then the rituals will take place…

1807
01:57:27,208 --> 01:57:29,541
and before you know it,
it'll all be over.

1808
01:57:31,125 --> 01:57:32,041
Cheers!

1809
01:57:55,541 --> 01:57:57,207
- Listen up, everybody!
- Yes?

1810
01:57:57,208 --> 01:57:58,999
We're playing <i>antakshari</i> now.

1811
01:57:59,000 --> 01:58:00,957
- No!
- Yes!

1812
01:58:00,958 --> 01:58:02,040
Please, please, please!

1813
01:58:02,041 --> 01:58:03,707
We're not going to play A for <i>antakshari.</i>

1814
01:58:03,708 --> 01:58:05,250
- Why?
- Because it's B for boring!

1815
01:58:07,083 --> 01:58:08,250
I know a game.

1816
01:58:08,958 --> 01:58:09,915
"Love check."

1817
01:58:09,916 --> 01:58:12,415
- Oh!
- Spicy.

1818
01:58:12,416 --> 01:58:13,374
Let's go.

1819
01:58:13,375 --> 01:58:16,458
Let's see how well the bride
and groom know each other.

1820
01:58:16,833 --> 01:58:18,791
Interesting. I like it.

1821
01:58:20,041 --> 01:58:21,582
- I'll ask the questions.
- Bring it on!

1822
01:58:21,583 --> 01:58:23,083
It's a rapid fire, so be quick.

1823
01:58:23,416 --> 01:58:24,666
- Ready?
- Bring it on.

1824
01:58:25,083 --> 01:58:26,166
Alright!

1825
01:58:27,166 --> 01:58:28,166
Diya's favorite color?

1826
01:58:28,750 --> 01:58:29,957
- Orange.
- Baby blue.

1827
01:58:29,958 --> 01:58:31,082
Baby blue?

1828
01:58:31,083 --> 01:58:32,750
- That was just the first answer!
- Minus one.

1829
01:58:32,875 --> 01:58:34,290
- Next one. Next one.
- Stupid question.

1830
01:58:34,291 --> 01:58:35,457
- They're still warming up.
- They can do it.

1831
01:58:35,458 --> 01:58:36,791
- First question.
- Once more.

1832
01:58:38,666 --> 01:58:39,832
Kunal's favorite food?

1833
01:58:39,833 --> 01:58:41,041
<i>- Chole bhature.
- Rajma… bhature.</i>

1834
01:58:41,333 --> 01:58:42,791
<i>Rajma bhature?!</i>

1835
01:58:43,166 --> 01:58:44,375
Innovation.

1836
01:58:44,500 --> 01:58:45,750
He's a <i>rajma</i> fan!

1837
01:58:46,958 --> 01:58:48,625
Let's get romantic.

1838
01:58:49,583 --> 01:58:50,665
Where was your first kiss?

1839
01:58:50,666 --> 01:58:51,833
- My…
- In the car, right?

1840
01:58:54,916 --> 01:58:56,625
Babe… bedroom.

1841
01:58:59,083 --> 01:59:01,750
Alright, let's make it simple.

1842
01:59:02,916 --> 01:59:04,375
Who said "I love you" first?

1843
01:59:04,500 --> 01:59:05,625
- She did.
- He…

1844
01:59:11,000 --> 01:59:13,583
Are you sure you've known
each other for 16 years?

1845
01:59:15,333 --> 01:59:18,541
Well, I guess that's the sign
of a successful relationship.

1846
01:59:19,291 --> 01:59:20,208
Confusion.

1847
01:59:25,125 --> 01:59:27,541
Okay, enough with this stupid game!

1848
01:59:27,916 --> 01:59:30,458
- Let's just play <i>antakshari.</i>
- Yes!

1849
01:59:30,625 --> 01:59:33,040
Two teams!
Team A and Team B.

1850
01:59:33,041 --> 01:59:34,125
- That's it.
- Okay, done.

1851
01:59:54,541 --> 01:59:56,041
I remembered all those things.

1852
01:59:57,916 --> 01:59:59,333
I don't know, in the moment…

1853
02:00:01,291 --> 02:00:02,166
I forgot.

1854
02:00:05,041 --> 02:00:11,000
<i>It's no good having you</i>

1855
02:00:11,458 --> 02:00:17,125
<i>If I don't have your whole heart</i>

1856
02:00:18,125 --> 02:00:24,707
<i>For this is love, you know</i>

1857
02:00:24,708 --> 02:00:30,333
<i>Not a prison sentence</i>

1858
02:00:31,166 --> 02:00:34,125
<i>Can putting it into words</i>

1859
02:00:34,541 --> 02:00:37,541
<i>Show you the pain in my heart?</i>

1860
02:00:37,833 --> 02:00:43,958
<i>Will I ever find a way
To tell it all to you?</i>

1861
02:00:44,375 --> 02:00:50,500
<i>Even if I'm never truly yours</i>

1862
02:00:51,000 --> 02:00:57,083
<i>Will you remember me by chance?</i>

1863
02:00:57,583 --> 02:01:03,458
<i>You…</i>

1864
02:01:04,375 --> 02:01:07,874
<i>I loved you while I lived and breathed</i>

1865
02:01:07,875 --> 02:01:13,500
<i>I'll love you after death</i>

1866
02:01:17,541 --> 02:01:24,250
<i>Even if fate keeps us apart
I'll love you my every breath</i>

1867
02:01:27,291 --> 02:01:34,000
<i>You can leave me</i>

1868
02:01:34,500 --> 02:01:38,583
<i>For somebody new</i>

1869
02:01:40,500 --> 02:01:47,166
<i>I'll accept it all</i>

1870
02:01:47,750 --> 02:01:52,375
<i>For the sake of you</i>

1871
02:01:53,416 --> 02:01:59,833
<i>Even through my tears
I'll try to make you smile</i>

1872
02:02:00,375 --> 02:02:07,041
<i>If I've chosen love
Then I must stand by it all the while</i>

1873
02:02:13,166 --> 02:02:19,250
<i>You are my whole life too</i>

1874
02:02:19,708 --> 02:02:25,833
<i>Every prayer came true for me</i>

1875
02:02:26,375 --> 02:02:32,458
<i>The day I found you</i>

1876
02:02:32,916 --> 02:02:39,000
<i>You…</i>

1877
02:02:39,750 --> 02:02:43,041
<i>I loved you while I lived and breathed</i>

1878
02:02:43,208 --> 02:02:49,583
<i>I'll love you after death</i>

1879
02:02:53,041 --> 02:02:59,583
<i>Even if fate keeps us apart
I'll love you my every breath</i>

1880
02:03:42,541 --> 02:03:43,833
Diya, you called me?

1881
02:03:45,958 --> 02:03:46,833
Wanted to give you this.

1882
02:03:48,958 --> 02:03:49,833
Why?

1883
02:03:50,416 --> 02:03:52,375
The wedding chain should stay
with the groom.

1884
02:03:52,791 --> 02:03:54,291
Otherwise, what'll he put around
the bride's neck?

1885
02:04:05,833 --> 02:04:07,291
It looked nice on her, right?

1886
02:04:11,125 --> 02:04:12,375
She'll have to wear it her whole life.

1887
02:04:13,958 --> 02:04:14,958
What are you saying?

1888
02:04:16,125 --> 02:04:17,416
Let's not do this, baby.

1889
02:04:19,916 --> 02:04:20,791
It's okay.

1890
02:04:21,791 --> 02:04:22,750
It really is.

1891
02:04:24,416 --> 02:04:25,416
You fell in love.

1892
02:04:26,708 --> 02:04:28,958
It really doesn't make you a bad person.

1893
02:04:31,250 --> 02:04:32,500
You didn't plan it.

1894
02:04:33,833 --> 02:04:35,166
In fact, this is my fault.

1895
02:04:35,791 --> 02:04:37,041
If I hadn't taken you to Sicily,

1896
02:04:37,583 --> 02:04:38,791
you would've never met Ally.

1897
02:04:39,750 --> 02:04:41,875
- Diya, it's not like that.
- Baby…

1898
02:04:42,666 --> 02:04:44,083
I know you well.

1899
02:04:45,583 --> 02:04:49,708
You avoid hurting people,
no matter what it costs you.

1900
02:04:50,125 --> 02:04:51,458
That's why I love you.

1901
02:04:53,333 --> 02:04:58,083
But don't marry me
out of a sense of responsibility

1902
02:04:58,958 --> 02:05:00,333
if your heart isn't in it.

1903
02:05:03,083 --> 02:05:04,125
Actually, you know what?

1904
02:05:06,666 --> 02:05:09,500
I've never seen you this unhappy.

1905
02:05:11,750 --> 02:05:13,750
I don't want to be the reason for that.

1906
02:05:15,625 --> 02:05:18,041
I only want to be the reason
for your happiness.

1907
02:05:19,208 --> 02:05:21,749
And if someone else gives
you that happiness,

1908
02:05:21,750 --> 02:05:23,041
how can I stop you?

1909
02:05:24,666 --> 02:05:26,291
And just because I love you,

1910
02:05:27,041 --> 02:05:30,374
and you can't tell me
you don't feel the same,

1911
02:05:30,375 --> 02:05:33,666
I can't pretend I don't know the truth.

1912
02:05:38,125 --> 02:05:39,041
Okay.

1913
02:05:47,708 --> 02:05:51,291
It feels like everyone here
already knows how I feel.

1914
02:05:52,625 --> 02:05:54,041
You've already decided

1915
02:05:55,541 --> 02:05:57,375
who I love and who I don't.

1916
02:06:06,083 --> 02:06:07,208
So you tell me.

1917
02:06:09,333 --> 02:06:10,333
Do you love her?

1918
02:06:34,166 --> 02:06:35,833
You know I love you.

1919
02:06:36,333 --> 02:06:38,665
I can see you love me.

1920
02:06:38,666 --> 02:06:40,540
- If you don't, then just say so.
- Ma'am!

1921
02:06:40,541 --> 02:06:41,832
- Like, why are you so scared?
- Excuse me, ma'am!

1922
02:06:41,833 --> 02:06:42,790
What?!

1923
02:06:42,791 --> 02:06:44,250
There's someone here to see you
at the reception.

1924
02:06:47,833 --> 02:06:48,875
Mom? Dad?

1925
02:06:49,208 --> 02:06:50,165
Hi, dear!

1926
02:06:50,166 --> 02:06:51,125
- Alisha!
- Hi!

1927
02:06:54,166 --> 02:06:55,582
What are you doing here?

1928
02:06:55,583 --> 02:06:57,416
Your friend Diya called us.

1929
02:06:57,833 --> 02:07:00,582
She said there was a big surprise.

1930
02:07:00,583 --> 02:07:02,291
And told us not to tell you.

1931
02:07:02,875 --> 02:07:05,416
So, what's the surprise?

1932
02:07:05,708 --> 02:07:06,583
Tell us.

1933
02:07:08,250 --> 02:07:09,416
I'll just be back.

1934
02:07:10,125 --> 02:07:11,000
- Alisha?
- Alisha?

1935
02:07:11,125 --> 02:07:12,166
That bitch!

1936
02:07:14,291 --> 02:07:15,250
What's happening?

1937
02:07:20,541 --> 02:07:21,874
Diya, what is going on?

1938
02:07:21,875 --> 02:07:23,625
Why did you call my parents?

1939
02:07:23,791 --> 02:07:25,250
- Listen--
- One second, Diya, please.

1940
02:07:27,250 --> 02:07:28,624
Let's just take this outside.

1941
02:07:28,625 --> 02:07:29,625
Wait, son.

1942
02:07:29,833 --> 02:07:31,708
- Diya!
- At least tell us what's going on.

1943
02:07:31,833 --> 02:07:34,999
- You say something!
- How can they do this to us now?

1944
02:07:35,000 --> 02:07:36,000
- How…
- Yeah…

1945
02:07:41,666 --> 02:07:43,041
She thinks…

1946
02:07:45,625 --> 02:07:46,791
I love you…

1947
02:07:48,875 --> 02:07:53,083
and I'm marrying her only
out of a sense of responsibility.

1948
02:07:54,375 --> 02:07:55,291
Am I wrong?

1949
02:08:02,375 --> 02:08:03,250
You're not.

1950
02:08:05,041 --> 02:08:06,083
But he'll never say it.

1951
02:08:06,833 --> 02:08:08,333
What if someone feels bad?

1952
02:08:08,583 --> 02:08:09,874
Someone's feelings get hurt?

1953
02:08:09,875 --> 02:08:12,208
- Someone's image gets ruined?
- I'm not talking to you.

1954
02:08:14,166 --> 02:08:15,500
Today he'll have to answer.

1955
02:08:15,708 --> 02:08:16,833
What do you want to hear?

1956
02:08:18,041 --> 02:08:19,916
You only wanna hear
what you wanna hear.

1957
02:08:36,875 --> 02:08:38,375
You still won't answer me?

1958
02:08:43,583 --> 02:08:45,291
Whose feelings are you protecting now?

1959
02:08:46,666 --> 02:08:49,916
At least respect me enough
to tell me the truth to my face.

1960
02:08:51,333 --> 02:08:54,000
Just tell me the truth,

1961
02:08:54,500 --> 02:08:56,000
and I'll leave happily.

1962
02:08:56,125 --> 02:08:57,166
Oh, please!

1963
02:08:57,291 --> 02:09:00,083
Stop acting like the victim.

1964
02:09:00,250 --> 02:09:01,875
And don't even talk about respect.

1965
02:09:02,125 --> 02:09:03,582
You respect him, right?

1966
02:09:03,583 --> 02:09:05,458
That's why you asked me to seduce him?

1967
02:09:06,625 --> 02:09:08,999
To test his loyalty?

1968
02:09:09,000 --> 02:09:10,541
Why didn't you ask him directly then?

1969
02:09:13,666 --> 02:09:16,375
Out of decency, I said nothing happened.

1970
02:09:16,916 --> 02:09:18,708
But it's not like nothing happened.

1971
02:09:19,125 --> 02:09:20,125
Tell him.

1972
02:09:20,416 --> 02:09:21,416
What is she talking about?

1973
02:09:22,000 --> 02:09:23,749
- Kunal…
- Tell him. Tell him the truth.

1974
02:09:23,750 --> 02:09:24,791
Is she telling the truth?

1975
02:09:28,666 --> 02:09:29,625
Kunal, baby…

1976
02:09:30,083 --> 02:09:32,291
Baby, I fucked up.

1977
02:09:32,791 --> 02:09:33,666
I'm sorry.

1978
02:09:34,041 --> 02:09:35,707
I just wanted to know

1979
02:09:35,708 --> 02:09:38,250
if you really wanted to be with me.

1980
02:09:40,500 --> 02:09:41,375
I'm sorry.

1981
02:09:42,333 --> 02:09:43,625
What happened was wrong.

1982
02:09:44,000 --> 02:09:46,499
I have no excuses.

1983
02:09:46,500 --> 02:09:48,540
But my intentions weren't bad.

1984
02:09:48,541 --> 02:09:50,750
- And you just played along?
- Only in the beginning.

1985
02:09:51,333 --> 02:09:53,708
Kunal, then-- Then I really
started feeling for you.

1986
02:09:53,875 --> 02:09:55,083
Everything was real.

1987
02:09:55,291 --> 02:09:57,124
- Every single bit of it, I swear.
- Kunal…

1988
02:09:57,125 --> 02:09:58,375
Kunal, just listen to me.

1989
02:09:58,708 --> 02:10:00,416
- Kunal, just listen to me!
- Don't even try!

1990
02:10:03,291 --> 02:10:04,166
Please.

1991
02:10:06,916 --> 02:10:12,041
<i>Every flaw in you</i>

1992
02:10:13,291 --> 02:10:19,083
<i>I'd still forgive</i>

1993
02:10:19,750 --> 02:10:25,208
<i>Even if it's wrong</i>

1994
02:10:26,208 --> 02:10:29,708
<i>- I'd relive it…</i>
- I won't say a word.

1995
02:10:30,166 --> 02:10:31,250
I'll keep quiet.

1996
02:10:32,125 --> 02:10:34,041
I can't leave you alone.

1997
02:10:35,791 --> 02:10:41,999
{\an8}<i>What can I do?
My love's gone wild</i>

1998
02:10:42,000 --> 02:10:48,625
<i>This is how my heart speaks its mind</i>

1999
02:10:48,875 --> 02:10:50,166
What did you gain from all this?

2000
02:10:51,625 --> 02:10:55,874
I called your parents here thinking
that if he admitted his feelings,

2001
02:10:55,875 --> 02:10:57,250
you two could finally be together!

2002
02:10:59,291 --> 02:11:02,249
I can really accept that
Kunal doesn't love me.

2003
02:11:02,250 --> 02:11:05,124
But if he also loses respect for me,

2004
02:11:05,125 --> 02:11:08,374
I swear to God, I will not forgive myself,
and I will not forgive you!

2005
02:11:08,375 --> 02:11:10,332
You could've told me
what you were doing!

2006
02:11:10,333 --> 02:11:11,665
Seeing Mom and Dad here suddenly,

2007
02:11:11,666 --> 02:11:14,374
I couldn't figure out your plan.
I panicked, man!

2008
02:11:14,375 --> 02:11:16,999
- You're such an idiot!
- I know! I know! I know!

2009
02:11:17,000 --> 02:11:19,040
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
I know it was our secret.

2010
02:11:19,041 --> 02:11:21,082
I shouldn't have told Kunal.

2011
02:11:21,083 --> 02:11:23,165
And now I know your
intentions weren't wrong.

2012
02:11:23,166 --> 02:11:24,583
Go tell him that!

2013
02:11:24,833 --> 02:11:27,249
He's not going to do
something stupid, right?

2014
02:11:27,250 --> 02:11:29,332
Why would he kill himself
over our stupidity?

2015
02:11:29,333 --> 02:11:30,290
Kill himself?!

2016
02:11:30,291 --> 02:11:32,332
What is wrong with you?
You jumped straight to suicide?!

2017
02:11:32,333 --> 02:11:33,915
Then what did you mean
by "do something stupid"?

2018
02:11:33,916 --> 02:11:35,957
I don't know! Stop yelling!
I'm freaking out!

2019
02:11:35,958 --> 02:11:37,124
You think I'm not freaking out?!

2020
02:11:37,125 --> 02:11:38,665
Ma'am, I'm here for the bride's makeup.

2021
02:11:38,666 --> 02:11:39,583
- Shut up!
- Shut up!

2022
02:11:49,750 --> 02:11:50,625
Where are you going?

2023
02:11:51,083 --> 02:11:52,208
To find him. Where else?

2024
02:11:52,666 --> 02:11:54,250
Why are you going? I'll go.

2025
02:11:54,500 --> 02:11:55,457
Why?

2026
02:11:55,458 --> 02:11:58,333
You already said you'd leave
if he admitted his feelings.

2027
02:11:58,750 --> 02:12:00,416
Well, did he admit it?
No, right?

2028
02:12:00,541 --> 02:12:02,374
- He didn't!
- You already know how he feels.

2029
02:12:02,375 --> 02:12:03,916
That's why you called my parents.

2030
02:12:04,291 --> 02:12:05,208
How noble of you!

2031
02:12:17,166 --> 02:12:20,000
I'm with him. Can't talk right now.

2032
02:12:23,125 --> 02:12:24,083
Oh, boy!

2033
02:12:28,875 --> 02:12:30,957
I'm with him. Can't talk.

2034
02:12:30,958 --> 02:12:32,416
We agreed you wouldn't say a word.

2035
02:12:33,250 --> 02:12:34,707
I'm not talking to you.

2036
02:12:34,708 --> 02:12:35,957
Hang up! Keep it down!

2037
02:12:35,958 --> 02:12:36,958
Fine.

2038
02:12:45,125 --> 02:12:46,000
Oh!

2039
02:12:47,708 --> 02:12:48,708
Give me the keys!

2040
02:12:49,375 --> 02:12:50,250
Whose car is it?

2041
02:12:54,583 --> 02:12:55,458
Open the door.

2042
02:12:56,458 --> 02:12:57,333
It's open.

2043
02:12:57,583 --> 02:12:58,624
Open the door.

2044
02:12:58,625 --> 02:12:59,916
Open!

2045
02:13:00,333 --> 02:13:01,208
Okay.

2046
02:13:01,625 --> 02:13:02,541
Fine.

2047
02:13:05,000 --> 02:13:05,958
You…

2048
02:13:06,750 --> 02:13:08,125
Diya!
Diya!

2049
02:13:13,333 --> 02:13:14,458
"Have a couple of drinks
and sleep it off."

2050
02:13:14,958 --> 02:13:16,750
"We'll play <i>antakshari</i> on the bus."

2051
02:13:17,333 --> 02:13:19,416
"Then all the rituals will happen.
It'll all be over before you know it."

2052
02:13:21,625 --> 02:13:22,791
Amazing father you are.

2053
02:13:23,458 --> 02:13:25,458
Why are you angry at me?
What did I do…

2054
02:13:26,458 --> 02:13:28,916
besides giving you good genes?

2055
02:13:29,958 --> 02:13:31,791
Two girls are fighting over you.

2056
02:13:50,708 --> 02:13:52,958
You know my intention
was never to hurt you.

2057
02:13:54,416 --> 02:13:55,333
I know.

2058
02:13:57,416 --> 02:13:58,749
He's just so lovable

2059
02:13:58,750 --> 02:14:01,291
that sacrificing a friendship
for him felt worth it.

2060
02:14:02,166 --> 02:14:05,500
Yeah, but you wouldn't do that
if you were me.

2061
02:14:11,291 --> 02:14:14,583
I'll never apologize for falling
in love with him.

2062
02:14:14,875 --> 02:14:16,708
- But for hurting you, I'm really--
- Drop it.

2063
02:14:19,625 --> 02:14:20,791
Doesn't suit you.

2064
02:14:29,125 --> 02:14:30,916
Whatever you decide,

2065
02:14:31,916 --> 02:14:33,041
hearts will be broken, son.

2066
02:14:35,625 --> 02:14:38,040
If you choose Diya,
Ally's heart will break.

2067
02:14:38,041 --> 02:14:40,708
If you choose Ally,
Diya's heart will break.

2068
02:14:41,958 --> 02:14:43,166
The family's hearts will break too.

2069
02:14:44,750 --> 02:14:46,000
Just don't break your own heart.

2070
02:14:47,750 --> 02:14:51,250
A man with a broken heart
can't keep anyone happy.

2071
02:14:53,833 --> 02:14:58,000
A broken heart makes life feel

2072
02:14:59,708 --> 02:15:00,875
unbearably heavy.

2073
02:15:12,625 --> 02:15:13,500
Get out.

2074
02:15:29,333 --> 02:15:30,208
Is that…

2075
02:15:30,583 --> 02:15:31,458
Yeah.

2076
02:15:32,708 --> 02:15:34,458
Where… where is he?

2077
02:15:35,000 --> 02:15:36,250
- Go, go, go!
- Yeah.

2078
02:15:48,416 --> 02:15:49,625
Kunal, stop the car!

2079
02:15:50,250 --> 02:15:51,125
Kunal!

2080
02:15:51,333 --> 02:15:52,208
Kunal!

2081
02:15:52,333 --> 02:15:53,582
Kunal, please stop the car!

2082
02:15:53,583 --> 02:15:54,790
Please stop the car!

2083
02:15:54,791 --> 02:15:55,666
- Kunal!
- Kunal!

2084
02:16:11,041 --> 02:16:13,791
<i>Eeny, meeny, miny, moe
Catch a tiger by the toe!</i>

2085
02:16:14,416 --> 02:16:15,291
Yeah?

2086
02:16:16,416 --> 02:16:18,000
No? Should we toss?

2087
02:16:19,458 --> 02:16:20,375
Got a coin?

2088
02:16:20,666 --> 02:16:21,833
Heads is her, tails is you.

2089
02:16:24,250 --> 02:16:25,333
Just answer me one thing, Diya.

2090
02:16:26,583 --> 02:16:27,666
Why'd you do it?

2091
02:16:28,750 --> 02:16:29,958
Just because of a joke?

2092
02:16:31,166 --> 02:16:32,832
You know why I could joke about it?

2093
02:16:32,833 --> 02:16:36,708
Because I never thought
you'd ever believe I'd cheat on you.

2094
02:16:39,500 --> 02:16:41,833
You broke my faith in us.

2095
02:16:42,166 --> 02:16:43,291
How did she ask you?

2096
02:16:45,166 --> 02:16:46,208
Jokingly?

2097
02:16:46,791 --> 02:16:47,750
To seduce me?

2098
02:16:48,666 --> 02:16:49,958
And you just laughed and agreed?

2099
02:16:52,958 --> 02:16:55,500
You both made me into a joke.

2100
02:17:04,125 --> 02:17:05,000
Sorry…

2101
02:17:14,083 --> 02:17:15,041
This is what happens

2102
02:17:15,416 --> 02:17:17,666
when people consume
too much social media nonsense.

2103
02:17:18,916 --> 02:17:21,041
"Couples should know everything
about each other."

2104
02:17:21,291 --> 02:17:23,250
"Give us five reasons
why you like each other."

2105
02:17:24,208 --> 02:17:26,583
"A relationship should
always remain exciting."

2106
02:17:27,666 --> 02:17:29,666
If excitement is what defines love,

2107
02:17:30,000 --> 02:17:31,750
then maybe love isn't that deep after all.

2108
02:17:34,666 --> 02:17:38,708
Every relationship feels exciting at first
because it's new.

2109
02:17:40,833 --> 02:17:43,999
New friends are fun too because
their stories are new to you.

2110
02:17:44,000 --> 02:17:46,125
Old friends' stories bore you
after a while.

2111
02:17:49,125 --> 02:17:51,083
You can be in love with anything
for a few days.

2112
02:17:53,791 --> 02:17:54,791
But, Diya…

2113
02:17:56,708 --> 02:17:58,375
love is like that worn-out T-shirt

2114
02:18:00,583 --> 02:18:02,583
you sleep best in.

2115
02:18:10,083 --> 02:18:11,000
And yes…

2116
02:18:12,208 --> 02:18:13,416
I do feel love for her.

2117
02:18:13,708 --> 02:18:14,625
She's lovely.

2118
02:18:17,666 --> 02:18:21,541
And maybe, in another life,
if we'd met sooner…

2119
02:18:24,458 --> 02:18:25,708
we could've been together.

2120
02:18:30,916 --> 02:18:31,916
But "maybe"

2121
02:18:33,416 --> 02:18:35,083
is a huge thing.

2122
02:18:37,583 --> 02:18:38,790
Maybe after six months,

2123
02:18:38,791 --> 02:18:40,250
we wouldn't even be able
to tolerate each other.

2124
02:18:43,833 --> 02:18:45,875
There's no "maybe" between her and me.

2125
02:18:46,916 --> 02:18:48,625
That's exactly why you and I are us, Diya.

2126
02:18:52,083 --> 02:18:52,958
You're like

2127
02:18:54,041 --> 02:18:56,541
my overflowing cupboard.

2128
02:18:56,666 --> 02:18:59,333
Mom sees it and says, "What a mess!"

2129
02:18:59,458 --> 02:19:01,750
But I can reach in blind

2130
02:19:04,166 --> 02:19:05,625
and find exactly what I need.

2131
02:19:07,416 --> 02:19:08,291
You know why?

2132
02:19:11,250 --> 02:19:12,541
Because it's my cupboard.

2133
02:19:15,166 --> 02:19:16,333
Yes, your kind of wedding…

2134
02:19:17,291 --> 02:19:18,708
is more my type.

2135
02:19:20,000 --> 02:19:22,250
And I'm doing this one for her.
Do you know why?

2136
02:19:22,375 --> 02:19:25,375
Because the wedding lasts four days, Ally.

2137
02:19:28,916 --> 02:19:30,875
But the relationship lasts a lifetime.

2138
02:19:34,250 --> 02:19:35,125
It's true

2139
02:19:36,291 --> 02:19:40,750
we don't know every tiny thing
about each other anymore, Diya.

2140
02:19:42,708 --> 02:19:43,916
But the big things?

2141
02:19:47,666 --> 02:19:49,041
We know them all.

2142
02:19:55,291 --> 02:19:56,250
Maybe today…

2143
02:19:57,916 --> 02:19:59,375
you like my smile more than she does.

2144
02:20:01,458 --> 02:20:02,333
But, Ally…

2145
02:20:04,708 --> 02:20:05,666
for years now…

2146
02:20:08,333 --> 02:20:10,250
she sees my tears

2147
02:20:11,458 --> 02:20:12,666
before they even reach my eyes.

2148
02:20:18,791 --> 02:20:22,833
You're that worn-out T-shirt
my sleep's gotten addicted to, Diya.

2149
02:20:26,083 --> 02:20:28,333
People unfairly judge habits.

2150
02:20:28,750 --> 02:20:29,708
Habits are a good thing.

2151
02:20:31,583 --> 02:20:33,333
They are built on trust.

2152
02:20:38,708 --> 02:20:40,291
You can become the sparkle in my eyes.

2153
02:20:43,750 --> 02:20:44,750
But she…

2154
02:20:46,833 --> 02:20:47,875
is my peace.

2155
02:20:57,708 --> 02:21:00,333
Yeah, she's a little crazy for testing me.

2156
02:21:01,625 --> 02:21:02,875
But you know what?

2157
02:21:03,583 --> 02:21:05,250
After all the madness
of mine you've tolerated…

2158
02:21:07,583 --> 02:21:08,458
you've earned the right.

2159
02:21:11,458 --> 02:21:14,875
You're not doing this just out of
a sense of responsibility, right?

2160
02:21:16,000 --> 02:21:16,875
I am.

2161
02:21:18,833 --> 02:21:20,916
It's responsibility, not a burden.

2162
02:21:21,541 --> 02:21:23,750
I want to be responsible for you, Diya.

2163
02:21:23,916 --> 02:21:24,958
That's why I'm doing this.

2164
02:21:26,500 --> 02:21:27,750
But there's one thing I'll never do.

2165
02:21:30,208 --> 02:21:32,625
I'll never tell you
what happened that night.

2166
02:21:35,708 --> 02:21:36,750
If you're still

2167
02:21:38,750 --> 02:21:40,250
willing to tolerate me,

2168
02:21:42,458 --> 02:21:43,833
then I'm around for this lifetime…

2169
02:21:46,583 --> 02:21:48,416
and all the lifetimes to come.

2170
02:21:58,125 --> 02:22:04,083
<i>You're the reason I still breathe</i>

2171
02:22:04,500 --> 02:22:09,583
<i>I live my life for you</i>

2172
02:22:10,791 --> 02:22:16,875
<i>How do I put in words</i>

2173
02:22:17,041 --> 02:22:22,125
<i>What I feel for you?</i>

2174
02:22:23,458 --> 02:22:29,416
<i>Nowhere in this world will anyone</i>

2175
02:22:29,750 --> 02:22:35,750
<i>- Ever love you…
- Quite this way</i>

2176
02:22:36,041 --> 02:22:41,916
<i>- No one else will…
- Give their heart</i>

2177
02:22:42,416 --> 02:22:47,291
<i>- Completely…
- Each passing day</i>

2178
02:22:54,916 --> 02:22:56,083
In this lifetime, he's yours.

2179
02:22:57,791 --> 02:22:59,000
In every lifetime, he's mine.

2180
02:23:01,541 --> 02:23:02,500
We'll see.

2181
02:23:29,208 --> 02:23:30,291
What are you guys waiting for?

2182
02:23:31,000 --> 02:23:32,291
We have a wedding to celebrate!

2183
02:23:37,250 --> 02:23:41,125
<i>These matters of fate</i>

2184
02:23:43,666 --> 02:23:47,666
<i>Only fate can explain</i>

2185
02:23:49,958 --> 02:23:55,125
<i>For me, without you</i>

2186
02:23:56,416 --> 02:24:01,166
<i>Nothing else remains</i>

2187
02:24:02,875 --> 02:24:08,041
<i>My eyes may fill with tears</i>

2188
02:24:09,333 --> 02:24:13,416
<i>But I'll hide all the pain</i>

2189
02:24:15,625 --> 02:24:18,791
<i>If you're happy</i>

2190
02:24:19,041 --> 02:24:21,416
<i>Then for your happiness</i>

2191
02:24:22,000 --> 02:24:26,958
<i>I'll celebrate the same</i>

2192
02:24:28,416 --> 02:24:33,791
<i>But I'll keep loving you</i>

2193
02:24:34,875 --> 02:24:40,041
<i>Forever and more</i>

2194
02:24:41,250 --> 02:24:46,583
<i>I'll die loving you</i>

2195
02:24:47,583 --> 02:24:53,375
<i>Forever and more</i>

2196
02:24:54,083 --> 02:24:56,708
<i>Forever and more</i>

2197
02:24:57,208 --> 02:25:00,083
<i>Forever and more</i>

2198
02:25:00,458 --> 02:25:05,666
<i>Forever and more</i>

2199
02:25:08,250 --> 02:25:11,791
<i>My friend…</i>

2200
02:25:15,625 --> 02:25:16,583
I can't.

2201
02:25:25,333 --> 02:25:26,333
I can't.

2202
02:25:44,000 --> 02:25:47,249
<i>Forever and more</i>

2203
02:25:47,250 --> 02:25:50,666
<i>My heartstrings are tied to you</i>

2204
02:26:07,750 --> 02:26:11,000
You know, I'd have no problem
marrying a divorced man.

2205
02:26:11,541 --> 02:26:14,250
So if things don't work out,
don't worry about it.

2206
02:26:14,416 --> 02:26:15,333
You've got me.

2207
02:26:15,875 --> 02:26:17,541
Babe, are you done?

2208
02:26:19,375 --> 02:26:20,291
Yeah.

2209
02:26:24,916 --> 02:26:25,957
Come on, fast.

2210
02:26:25,958 --> 02:26:27,000
Come fast, come.